.TH NETMON-UNINSTALL 1 "November 2026" "NetMon 1.1.22" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netmon-uninstall \- guided removal utility for NetMon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netmon-uninstall
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netmon-uninstall
opens an interactive terminal workflow for removing the NetMon package and,
only after explicit confirmation, optional NetMon configuration or runtime
data. User data is not removed by the Debian package's normal removal scripts.
.SH PACKAGE AND USER TARGETS
The package target is fixed to netmon. Caller overrides of NETMON_PACKAGE,
HOME and XDG_DOCUMENTS_DIR do not select privileged removal targets.
The invoking account is checked against the system account database; its home
directory is obtained from that database. User-file cleanup runs with that
account's permissions in a clean environment. Root-account user data is retained.
Only Documents and Dokumente below that home are considered automatically;
custom or external document locations require separate manual review.
The final summary displays the package, account, home and requested file targets.
Symlink redirects and paths outside the verified home are refused.
.SH WIREGUARD OWNERSHIP
Automatic NetworkManager cleanup requires a protected NetMon creation receipt,
an unchanged root-owned keyfile, and a matching WireGuard UUID. The current
names and exact UUIDs are displayed for separate confirmation. User profile
JSON, connection names and user-supplied ownership markers grant no authority.
Connections from older installations or changed profiles are retained. There
is no automatic adoption or force-cleanup option; an administrator must review
and separately approve any manual deletion by exact UUID.
User VPN-file cleanup retains system WireGuard configurations. The separate
test-system option to delete all WireGuard configurations is intentionally
destructive and must not be used as a NetMon ownership check.
.SH WARNING
Review every prompt before confirming optional cleanup. WireGuard, DNS,
NetworkManager, and user-data cleanup choices can affect system configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR netmon (1),
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR apt (8)
